  "findings": [
    "Both source prefabs schedule Destroy after one scaled second; copied production wrappers remove the behaviour before any Start executes.",
    "Both contain FadeLight that destroys its object. All point lights and demo behaviours removed only from derived wrappers.",
    "Ice contains two looping five-second emitters with 1000-particle default caps; production wrappers make finite bounded bursts.",
    "Source parent scale3 normalizes to1. Production cell factors Ice0.66/Fire1.18 preserve relative birth layout.",
    "BuiltIn soft-particle depth code has no orthographic branch. Derived materials disable SOFTPART_ON and DEPTHGLOW_ON without changing vendor shaders.",
    "Custom1 alpha vertex streams and source module curves remain on the corresponding renderers.",
    "No component changes gameplay. Pool lifetime uses scaled deltaTime, pauses on gameplay Pause and clears on board exits.",
    "Vendor shader include uses texture sampling/math only; no runtime MonoBehaviour dependency."
  ]
